<Layout
  title={"RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise"}
  description={"About RCE-JEPA. World Coding is the subject; JEPA is the premise. Reports measured H1, H2 (C_check / E_model = 0.000582 on M5 Max), H7, H8, H14, H15 + FormJEPA-v1 (8.42M params, 22/40 k=1, 27/40 k=16 at 58.65–474.76 mJ RAPL core reported_j) + Shape D Gear-0 + 3-Gear Cascade (8.70x Zipf frontier-call reduction), and 151-task rce repair rung f promotion audit."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research paper · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      RCE-JEPA: World Coding, with JEPA as Premise
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      RCE-JEPA (RCE is the Reality Code Engine; JEPA is a Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) keeps its name. The subject is World Coding. JEPA is the premise: predict a compact summary of a program instead of the next word-piece of text. The proposer slot is any learned model over Forms. The checker decides. The Laws of Coding are the acceptance rule under test.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What it claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>It states a thesis, fifteen hypotheses (H1 to H15) and six falsifiers (RJ-F1 to RJ-F6). Measured deterministic floors: median rho <code>9.34</code> over 185 hand-written programs (H1); <code>0</code> invariant violations in 1,275 fuzzed mutants (H7); <code>0</code> replay mismatches on 10,500 streams across six targets (H8); and the plain arm of ladder run 3 closing <code>111</code> of <code>151</code> tasks (<code>73.5%</code>) at zero model calls, leaving <code>40</code> real-history residual tasks (H14 supported).</li>
        <li>At <code>openIE-dev/rce</code> commit <code>1762fb4b</code> (<code>reported_j</code>; <code>measured_j = None</code>, <code>board_metered = false</code>): <strong>H2 is supported</strong> on Apple M5 Max (<code>C_check / E_model = 0.04904 J / 84.25 J = 0.000582 &lt;= 0.05</code>, <code>1,718×</code> cheaper). Across the <strong>40 open residual tasks</strong> (<strong>H15</strong>), off-the-shelf <code>k = 1</code> proposers admit <code>34/40</code> (<code>Claude Opus 5.5</code>), <code>32/40</code> (<code>Claude Sonnet 5.5</code>), <code>31/40</code> (<code>xAI Grok 4.20 Reasoning</code>), <code>29/40</code> (<code>OpenAI GPT-OSS-120B</code>), <code>27/40</code> (local <code>Qwen 3.6 35B-A3B</code> at <code>124.8 J</code>/admitted), and <code>17/40</code> (<code>DeepSeek V4.1</code>), while the first purpose-trained latent Form JEPA repair proposer <strong><code>FormJEPA-v1</code></strong> (<code>8.42M</code> trainable parameters over <code>1,387</code> disjoint Form shapes, zero evaluation overlap) admits <code>177/200</code> held-out synthetic Form defects and closes <code>22/40</code> (<code>k = 1</code>) and <code>27/40</code> (<code>k = 16</code>, matching <code>Qwen 3.6 35B-A3B</code>) on H15 at <code>58.65 mJ</code> / <code>474.76 mJ</code> RAPL core <code>reported_j</code> (<code>1.19 J</code> / <code>6.74 J</code> gross package).</li>
        <li>Combining <strong>Shape D (<code>DNULLMM1</code>) Gear-0</strong> (<code>34/40</code> replay at <code>0</code> calls, <code>0.325 µs</code> / <code>1.77 µJ</code> per probe, <code>7/9</code> alpha-renamed hits) with <strong>Gear 1 (<code>FormJEPA-v1 k = 16</code>)</strong> and <strong>Gear 2 (<code>Opus 5.5</code>)</strong> cuts 200-arrival <code>Zipf(0.85)</code> frontier calls from <code>200</code> (stateless) and <code>48</code> (2-Gear) to <strong><code>23</code> (<code>8.70×</code> reduction)</strong>, and the 151-task <code>rce repair</code> rung <code>f</code> audit records <code>3/119 = 2.5% &gt; 2.0%</code> stochastic closes (<code>3/3</code> passing <code>W-MUT-1</code>, <code>0</code> contradictions), confirming rung <code>f</code> stays in <code>observe</code> mode. Honest boundary: open multi-module API synthesis still requires Gear-2 frontier proposers, full intent-to-Form synthesis (H3) and calibrated energy ranking (H5, H11) remain open, and remote cloud server joules remain <code>not_available</code>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><picture><source type="image/svg+xml" srcset="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.svg" /><img src="/figures/rce-jepa/architecture.png" alt="The proposed RCE-JEPA pipeline: intent to a latent point, decoded to candidate Forms, each admitted by the checker or reported as requiring change." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The proposed pipeline. Any learned proposer may suggest a Form. JEPA, predicting in a latent space, is the instance drawn. The checker admits each candidate or reports that it requires change, naming the rule.</figcaption>
    </figure>

